-- service_role INSERT on resume_documents.
--
-- WHY. 20260812231617 granted resume_documents select/insert/delete to
-- authenticated (the browser uploads a resume as the candidate, under RLS) and
-- only select to service_role (added later, for the server-side reads). That
-- was correct while the only writer was the candidate's own browser.
--
-- Tailored resumes are different: they are generated by the server, which runs
-- as service_role, so it has to insert the row that records the generated file.
-- service_role bypasses RLS but NOT table privileges, so without this the
-- insert fails with "permission denied for table resume_documents" — the same
-- failure mode 20260917150000 documents for candidate_profiles.
--
-- INSERT only, deliberately. Nothing server-side updates or deletes a resume
-- document; deletion stays with the candidate's own session (lib/resume.ts
-- deleteResume), where RLS scopes it to their own rows. Adding w or d here
-- would give the server delete rights over the candidate's uploads for no
-- reason any caller has.
grant insert on public.resume_documents to service_role;
